.TH NETCUP\-CLI 1 "October 2026" "netcup-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netcup\-cli \- Command\-line client for the Netcup Server Control Panel (SCP) REST API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netcup\-cli
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netcup\-cli
manages Netcup VPS servers via the SCP REST API.
Authentication uses the OIDC device\-code flow — no password is required.
Credentials (refresh token) are stored in
.I ~/.config/netcup\-cli/credentials.json
(mode 0600).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output raw JSON instead of formatted tables.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help for any command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Authentication
.TP
.B netcup\-cli login
Authenticate via OIDC device\-code flow. Opens a browser URL; no password needed.
.TP
.B netcup\-cli logout
Remove locally saved credentials (does not revoke the token).
.TP
.B netcup\-cli whoami
Show whether credentials are stored locally.
.SS Server Management
.TP
.B netcup\-cli list
List all servers (ID, nickname, hostname, template, status).
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli info " SERVER
Show server details: state, vCPUs, RAM, disks, and a full interface table
(MAC, IPv4, IPv6 prefix, VLAN, monthly traffic).
.I SERVER
may be a numeric ID, nickname, or hostname.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli start " SERVER " [" \-\-yes ]
Start a server. Prompts for confirmation unless
.B \-\-yes
is given.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli stop " SERVER " [" \-\-yes ]
Gracefully stop a server.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli reset " SERVER " [" \-\-yes ]
Hard\-reset (reboot) a server.
.SS VNC Console
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli vnc " SERVER
Open the SCP web console for a server in the default browser.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli vnc " SERVER " \-\-url\-only"
Print the VNC URL without opening a browser.
.SS Snapshots
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli snapshot list " SERVER
List snapshots for a server.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli snapshot create " SERVER " \-\-name " NAME
Create a snapshot.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli snapshot delete " SERVER " " SNAPSHOT_ID " [" \-\-yes ]
Delete a snapshot. Cannot be undone.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli snapshot restore " SERVER " " SNAPSHOT_ID " [" \-\-yes ]
Restore a server from a snapshot. All current disk data will be lost.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli snapshot export " SERVER " " SNAPSHOT_ID
Export a snapshot.
.SS OS Images
.TP
.B netcup\-cli images
List available OS images. Uses the first server on the account to determine
available images (images are architecture\-specific).
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli images " SERVER
List OS images available for a specific server.
.TP
.B netcup\-cli images \-\-all
Include deprecated images in the listing.
.SS Installation
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli install " SERVER
Interactive wizard to reinstall a server with a new OS.
Prompts for: image, hostname, locale, timezone, user, password,
SSH keys, SSH password auth, custom post\-install script, and e\-mail notification.
.B WARNING:
The target disk is formatted; all data will be lost.
.PP
Non\-interactive example:
.RS
.nf
netcup\-cli install Mia \\
  \-\-image 1234 \\
  \-\-hostname mia.example.com \\
  \-\-locale de_DE.UTF\-8 \\
  \-\-timezone Europe/Berlin \\
  \-\-username admin \\
  \-\-ssh\-key 456 \\
  \-\-no\-ssh\-password \\
  \-\-script ./post\-install.sh \\
  \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.SS SSH Keys
.TP
.B netcup\-cli ssh\-key list
List all SSH keys on the account.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli ssh\-key add " NAME " " PUBKEY_FILE
Upload an SSH public key from a file.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli ssh\-key add " NAME " \-\-key " "\"ssh\-ed25519 AAAA...\""
Upload an SSH public key from a string.
.TP
.BI "netcup\-cli ssh\-key delete " KEY_ID " [" \-\-yes ]
Delete an SSH key. May remove server access.
.SS Reverse DNS
.TP
.B netcup\-cli rdns ipv4 get|set|delete \fIIP\fR
Manage IPv4 reverse DNS.
.TP
.B netcup\-cli rdns ipv6 get|set|delete \fIIP\fR
Manage IPv6 reverse DNS.
.SS Tasks
.TP
.B netcup\-cli tasks list|get|cancel
List, inspect, or cancel asynchronous API tasks.
.SS Shell Completion
.TP
.B netcup\-cli completion bash
Print Bash completion script. Add to shell config with:
.BR "eval \(dq$(netcup\-cli completion bash)\(dq"
.TP
.B netcup\-cli completion zsh
Print Zsh completion script.
.TP
.B netcup\-cli completion fish
Print Fish completion script.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/netcup\-cli/credentials.json
Stored refresh token (mode 0600). Never contains passwords or access tokens.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NETCUP_OIDC_CLIENT_ID
Override the OIDC client ID (default:
.IR scp ).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the base directory for credential storage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# First login
netcup\-cli login

# List servers and open VNC for one
netcup\-cli list
netcup\-cli vnc Mia

# Reinstall with Ubuntu (interactive)
netcup\-cli install Mia

# Create a snapshot before upgrading
netcup\-cli snapshot create Mia \-\-name pre\-upgrade

# JSON output for scripting
netcup\-cli \-\-json list | jq '.[].id'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Netcup SCP Web UI: https://www.servercontrolpanel.de
.br
Source: https://github.com/Maxsander123/netcup\-cli
.SH AUTHOR
